From 7232805547915dcbca2409588a89092417251b6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivy Evans <ivy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:53:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] tslpatcher: run the mod's nwnnsscomp.exe off Windows
 through a launcher

HoloPatcher compiles a [CompileList] with the nwnnsscomp.exe the mod
ships only on Windows; anywhere else it uses the built-in compiler, so
the same mod installs different bytecode depending on the platform, and
the built-in compiler's defects reach the game (engine-call arguments
were pushed in reverse from December 2025 until the previous commit).

PYKOTOR_NWNNSSCOMP_LAUNCHER names a command line nwnnsscomp's is
appended to (for instance "wine", or a script that runs Wine in a
container); with it set, the mod's compiler runs on any platform, with
the same TSLPatcher-version check and the same fallback as on Windows.
PYKOTOR_NWNNSSCOMP_TIMEOUT overrides the five seconds a compile may
take, which a Wine start alone can use up.

Measured: Alignment Affects Force Powers' k_fp_heal1ti.nss, compiled by
its own nwnnsscomp.exe under Wine through this path, is byte-identical
to the same compiler's output on the game's own machine.
